 23\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$"] [:db/cas 17592186269153 :question/worked-solution "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=[\\begin{aligned}{3}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {2}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {2}^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}9 & 27 \\\\ -4 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}17 & 23 \\\\ 23 & 85\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 23\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=17+85+13=115.\n$$" "To get the normal equation corresponding to $W\\,Ax=Wb,$ we pre-multiply both sides of the equation by $(W\\,A)^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot W\\,Ax & =(W\\,A)^{T}\\cdot Wb \\\\ {A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)Ax & ={A}^{T}({W}^{T}W)b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\n{W}^{T}W=\\begin{bmatrix}{3}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {2}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & {2}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nour normal equation can be written as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 27 \\\\ -4 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}17 & 23 \\\\ 23 & 85\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ 23\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=17+85+13=115.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186269154 :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,W=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $W,$ and the vector $b$ above. If the normal equation for the corresponding weighted least-squares problem $W\\,Ax=Wb$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & 36 \\\\ 36 & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,W=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $W,$ and the vector $b$ above. If the normal equation for the corresponding weighted least-squares problem $W\\,Ax=Wb$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}a & 36 \\\\ 