es below. Find an expression for the vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}$ that best fits the data. \n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & {0}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 6 & {6}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 8 & {8}^{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\beta =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,y=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186269251 :question/problem "| $x$ | **$1$** | **$3$** | **$5$** | **$7$** | **$9$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $3$ | $-3$ | $2$ |\n\nConsider the data above and the matrices below. Find an expression for the vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}$ that best fits the data. \n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & {1}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5 & {5}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 7 & {7}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 9 & {9}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,\\beta =[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "| $x$ | **$1$** | **$3$** | **$5$** | **$7$** | **$9$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $3$ | $-3$ | $2$ |\n\nConsider the data above and the matrices below. Find an expression for the vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}$ that best fits the data. \n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & {1}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5 & {5}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 7 & {7}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 9 & {9}^{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\beta =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,y=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186269252 :question/problem "| $x$ | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** | **$6$** | **$7$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $2$ | $0$ | $2$ | $-3$ |\n\nConsider the data above and the matrices below. Find an expression for the vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}$ that best fits the data. \n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & {3}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5 & {5}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 6 & {6}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 7 & {7}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,\\beta =[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "| $x$ | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** | **$6$** | **$7$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $2$ | $0$ | $2$ | $-3$ |\n\nConsider the data above and the matrices below. Find an expression for the vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}$ that best fits the data. \n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & {3}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5 & {5}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 6 & {6}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 7 & {7}^{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\beta =\\begin{bmatrix}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,y=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186269254 :question/problem "| $x$ | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** | **$6$** | **$7$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $-2$ | $3$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nConsider the data above and the matrices below. Find an expression for the vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}+{\\beta }_{3}{x}^{3}$ that best fits the data. \n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & {3}^{2} & {3}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} & {4}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 5 & {5}^{2} & {5}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 6 & {6}^{2} & {6}^{3} \\\\ 1 & 7 & {7}^{2} & {7}^{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,\\beta =[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "| $x$ | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** | **$6$** | **$7$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $-2$ | $3$ | $0